From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: clock: mediatek: add the MT6897 camera clock gates

Add the camsys_main and cam_vcore clock gate blocks of the MediaTek MT6897
camera, with their clock identifiers. The identifiers follow the tables of
the MediaTek vendor driver (OnePlus Pad GPL release, clk-mt6897-cam.c).

Like the video encoder blocks, they carry no power-domains property: the
CAM_VCORE and CAM_MAIN power domains take gates of these blocks to come
up, so a power domain and its clock controller would wait for each other.
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
index 2db4978f7..993dbf842 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     items:
       - enum:
+          - mediatek,mt6897-cam-vcore
+          - mediatek,mt6897-camsys-main
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-c
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-en
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-es
diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.h b/include/dt-bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.h
index e69935329..a03a14992 100644
--- a/include/dt-bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.h
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.h
@@ -573,4 +573,39 @@
 #define CLK_VEN2_CKE5_GALS		5
 #define CLK_VEN2_CKE6_GALS_SRAM		6
 
+/* CAMSYS_MAIN */
